{
  "requirement": "Overrides the SDK’s OpenAI model, endpoint, credentials, or inference options. Omitted settings use the defaults in the agent configuration contract.\n\n```rust,ignore\n#[non_exhaustive]\npub struct OpenAiConfig {\n    pub model: Option<String>,\n    pub endpoint: Option<String>,\n    pub api_key_env: Option<String>,\n    pub api_key: Option<SecretString>,\n    pub options: BTreeMap<String, OptionValue>,\n}\n\nimpl OpenAiConfig {\n    pub fn new() -> Self;\n    pub fn model(self, model: String) -> Self;\n    pub fn endpoint(self, endpoint: String) -> Self;\n    pub fn api_key_env(self, api_key_env: String) -> Self;\n    pub fn api_key(self, api_key: SecretString) -> Self;\n    pub fn option(self, key: String, value: OptionValue) -> Self;\n}\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl Clone for OpenAiConfig;\nimpl Debug for OpenAiConfig;\nimpl Default for OpenAiConfig;\nimpl<'de> Deserialize<'de> for OpenAiConfig;\nimpl PartialEq for OpenAiConfig;\nimpl Serialize for OpenAiConfig;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests adequately check `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.OpenAiConfig`. I did not read the implementation. I read the sibling requirement `agent_config.settings` for the default values.\n\nObligations and the tests that cover them:\n\n- **Struct shape, `new()`, and builders.** `backend_builders_set_only_the_requested_fields` in `config.rs` checks that `OpenAiConfig::new()` serializes to `{}`. It then applies `model`, `endpoint`, `api_key_env`, `api_key` and `option`, and asserts the full serialized object. A repeated `option` key replaces the earlier value, and the other options stay in place.\n- **Serialize and Deserialize, PartialEq, nested options.** `all_backends_preserve_nested_settings_and_credentials` round-trips an OpenAI config through JSON, checking the value, the string form and `PartialEq` equality. `openai_inference_options_only_fill_missing_defaults` checks that `{\"backend\":\"openai\"}` deserializes to `AgentConfig::OpenAi(OpenAiConfig::new())`.\n- **Defaults for omitted settings.**\n  - Model and endpoint: `option_defaults_and_credential_resolution_are_deterministic` asserts `gpt-6.1-sol` and `https://api.openai.com/v1` for `OpenAiConfig::default()`. That test also covers `Default`.\n  - Default credential variable: `openai_uses_the_default_credential_variable` runs a child process with `OPENAI_API_KEY` set and asserts the resolved key.\n  - Default options: `max_output_tokens` is 16384 and `reasoning.effort` is `low`. User-supplied options override only the missing defaults, including merging a partial `reasoning` map.\n- **Overrides.**\n  - `api_key_env`: a missing environment variable produces an error naming it.\n  - `api_key`: an explicit key takes precedence over a missing variable.\n  - Empty and missing environment values are rejected in the `credential` helper tests.\n  - Model, endpoint and key overrides: `supplied_openai_backend_runs_independent_calls_against_a_local_transport` in `configured.rs` runs against a local transport. It asserts the request model `local-test`, the default `max_output_tokens`, and that the key is not persisted.\n- **Public surface.** `public_exports_match_the_appendix` in `tests/public_api.rs` checks the exports against rustdoc.\n\nThe `Clone`, `Debug` and `#[non_exhaustive]` items are derives or compile-time attributes with no conditional or transformation of their own. The requirement text states no behavior for them, so they need no separate test. I found no plausible requirement-violating behavior that these tests would accept.",
  "references": "1e27ef26f764835e7d12b55c94dc204c3b3fe9b16be8fc68565e50322e5ce3e9",
